From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] cuda/hip: RDNA4 DPP scan + multi-warp token chunking in mm_ids_helper

mm_ids_helper (4.5% of pp512 kernel time after the 0026-state profile,
48.1us avg at 512 tokens) runs one warp per expert with a serial loop
over all tokens. Each 4-token iteration issues seven __shfl-class ops -
warp_reduce_any<8>, a 3-step __shfl_up scan over the 8-lane token
groups, and a final broadcast - and on gfx1201 every one lowers to
ds_bpermute_b32 behind a full s_wait_dscnt: ~900 serialized LDS
round-trips per block at 512 tokens. The same pathology the 0026 patch
removed from gated_delta_net.

Two changes:

1. RDNA4 wave32 DPP forms (guarded to gfx120x, generic path untouched):
   the 8-lane any-reduce becomes quad_perm xor1/xor2 + row_half_mirror
   ORs, and the group scan + total broadcast become row_shr:8/row_shl:8
   partial sums combined through one v_permlanex16 - VALU-only, no LDS,
   no waits. The trailing nex_prev warp_reduce_sum uses the 0026-style
   5-op DPP butterfly.

2. Multi-warp token chunking (all archs, engaged at n_tokens >= 128):
   the serial token loop splits into nwarps=4 contiguous chunks, each
   warp compacting its chunk into a disjoint shared-memory slice; the
   per-warp counts and nex_prev partials merge through 2*nwarps ints of
   shared memory after one __syncthreads. Chunks are contiguous, so the
   concatenated slices ARE the single-warp output: the kernel is pure
   integer bookkeeping and the result is bit-identical by construction.
   nwarps=8 measured slightly worse (12.1us vs 10.7us), decode-sized
   calls (n_tokens < 128) keep the single-warp launch.

Measured on the R9700 box (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M, HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0):

- kernel: mm_ids_helper<8> 48.12us -> 10.68us avg at pp512 (4.5x),
  4.62% -> 1.04% of pp512 kernel time (rocprofv3, 240 calls).
- model (5-round interleaved whole-process A/B vs the 26-patch control
  binary): pp512 4054.0 -> 4183.8 (+3.20%), arms fully separated;
  tg128 119.99 vs 119.98 (flat). pp16384 2791 -> 2840 (+1.8%).
- correctness: test-backend-ops MUL_MAT_ID all OK at nwarps 1/4/8
  (the qwen3-moe cases n_mats=128/n_used=8/bs up to 512 exercise the
  DPP + chunked path); server greedy identity vs control BYTE-EXACT
  (integer kernel, no float change); ppl 3.9251/3.9304/3.9271 vs
  control cluster 3.9257-3.9292 on the same session (stock 3.9314,
  all deltas within +-0.16%).
